# Procedural UI System (Sanitized Backup)

This backup retains high-level guidance for the procedural UI helpers while removing confidential implementation specifics.

## Overview
- Procedural UI sprites assemble widget geometry from primitive shapes and respond to basic interaction events.
- Generators consume stencil descriptors and active theme data to keep overlays visually consistent.
- Callback routing, theming heuristics, and asset bindings are [REDACTED].

## ProceduralUIGenerator
- Listens for descriptors, resolves style information, and produces sprites ready for immediate use or deferred retrieval.
- Supports configurable dimensions, interaction hooks, and automatic cleanup.
- Descriptor parsing, batching policies, and dependency injection details are [REDACTED].

## UIShapeRegistry
- Stores reusable shape builders for widgets rendered with SDF techniques.
- Provides canonical identifiers for rounded rectangles, toggles, sliders, and similar elements.
- Shape tessellation parameters, vendor integrations, and shader bindings are [REDACTED].

## Usage Notes
- Scenes load default shapes, request generated sprites as needed, and render them via the shared procedural pipeline.
- Additional notes on renderer integration, licensing, and proprietary datasets are [REDACTED].
